furicam (1.5.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Camera: revert the async open/close to synchronous — the measured open cost
    is 390ms, not the overstated figure it was justified on, and the worker
    thread ordering surfaced a whole class of latent races: a frozen exposure
    cache, a stranded "cannot open camera" on a fast flip, and 90°-skewed photo
    orientation.  A single-threaded open has no cross-thread ordering bugs by
    construction, so the flip, exposure and rotation issues are gone at the root
  * Camera: keep the preview result callback on applyControlsToActive and after
    an HDR burst — the exposure cache now tracks the live scene, so the first
    shot after a lighting change is exposed correctly (HDR base included)
  * Pro mode: snap the shutter slider to a ½-stop standard ladder (1/1000…1/3
    plus the max-exposure cap) — even travel per stop, true 1/60 (was 1/58), no
    "1/Infinity" dead zone at the fast end
  * UI: make HDR mutually exclusive with pro mode and with RAW (RAW+HDR produced
    no usable DNGs; pro+HDR contradict on exposure control)
  * UI: fix the HDR "Hold still/Processing" badge overlapping the zoom slider,
    stop the settings arrow overlapping the recording timer, and recolor the
    gray-on-gray gallery play/resume icons white

 -- nico359 <124350776+nico359@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:40:00 +0200

furicam (1.5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * HDR: stop the burst's own +3EV frame from feeding the cached base exposure
    — a second HDR shot no longer computes its EV0/+3 from the previous
    bracket's longest exposure and comes out far too bright
  * Gallery: retry the deferred video-thumbnail probe instead of dropping it —
    the review button now shows a thumbnail right after recording stops, not
    only after reopening the app
  * Camera: fix two races from the async-open work — the camera list no longer
    shows every camera twice (concurrent enumerate), and switching to the
    selfie camera no longer intermittently fails with "cannot open camera"
    (close→open device-teardown race; retry the transient busy status)

