furicam (1.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Camera: add pixel-art (Pixless-style) photo filters with a live GLSL preview
    (pixelate + palette quantize) and matching saved photos; six bundled lospec
    palettes plus a no-palette auto mode, selectable in settings.  The preview
    filter is disabled whenever the output bypasses it (RAW, HDR, video mode)
  * Camera: flash overhaul — AF-assisted flash capture (torch lights for focus
    before the pulse), a video-mode torch toggle, and a fix for the flash mode
    not applying on startup.  Auto and On flash now share the same focus timing,
    and tap-to-focus uses the assist light in both modes
  * Video: native 16:9 preview stream so the viewfinder shows the full recording
    FOV (was cropped tighter than the clip)
  * Video: brighter low-light recording — let the frame rate drop in the dark
    instead of pinning it (this HAL caps AE at ISO 961)
  * Video: fix the record button not showing the stop-square (declarative state
    now), and add an elapsed-time indicator while recording
  * Build: experimental Flatpak manifest and configurable CMake install paths

